From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: mux the camera master clock
 and fix its GPIOs

The rear OV5648 never acknowledged a single I2C transaction, because two
things were wrong at once.

CLK_CIF_OUT was named as the sensor's clock, but nothing ever muxed it onto
its pin: the node's pinctrl-0 listed only the two GPIOs, so GPIO4_C0 kept
its default function and the sensor had no XVCLK.

The reset and powerdown GPIOs were taken from the schematic's net names,
which are swapped with respect to the camera connector. Measured by driving
each of the four candidate lines through every combination with the clock
running and probing the bus:

  OV5648  (0x36) answers 0x56/0x48 iff GPIO4_B0 and GPIO4_B2 are released
  GC02M2  (0x37) answers 0x02      iff GPIO4_B3 is released
  GPIO4_B1 has no observable effect

So CAMERAF_RST_L and CAMERAF_PDN_L drive the *rear* sensor (connector pins
MIPI-RST and PDN1-B) and CAMERAB_PDN_L enables the front one, the opposite
of what the net names suggest.

Gating each clkout separately confirms CIF_CLKOUT is the single master clock
shared by both sensors; CAM_CLKOUT0 is not connected:

  only CAM_CLKOUT0: neither sensor answers
  only CIF_CLKOUT:  both answer

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN f1_a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi f1_b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 09:29:58.349923749 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi	2026-09-18 09:29:58.349971750 +0200
@@ -616,7 +616,15 @@
 		compatible = "ovti,ov5648";
 		reg = <0x36>;
 		pinctrl-names = "default";
-		pinctrl-0 = <&camerab_pdn_l &camerab_rst_l>;
+		/*
+		 * The schematic's net names are swapped with respect to the
+		 * camera connector: CAMERAF_RST_L and CAMERAF_PDN_L reach the
+		 * *rear* sensor (connector pins MIPI-RST and PDN1-B), while
+		 * CAMERAB_PDN_L enables the front one. CIF_CLKOUT is the
+		 * single master clock shared by both sensors, and nothing
+		 * muxed it onto its pin at all.
+		 */
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cameraf_pdn_l &cameraf_rst_l &cif_clk>;
 
 		clocks = <&cru CLK_CIF_OUT>;
 		assigned-clocks = <&cru CLK_CIF_OUT>;
@@ -625,8 +633,8 @@
 		avdd-supply = <&vcc2v8_dvp>;
 		dvdd-supply = <&vdd1v2_dvp>;
 		dovdd-supply = <&vcc1v8_dvp>;
-		powerdown-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
-		reset-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB1 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		powerdown-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB2 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio4 RK_PB0 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		port {
 			ov5648_out: endpoint {
